{
  "_doc": [
    "The equipment palette (build.mjs 'equip' job). Every KayKit adventurer texture is a 8x4 grid of",
    "vertical colour ramps (light at the top, dark at the bottom). 'swatchRoles' names what each used",
    "swatch is on that model's meshes, so the client can recolour by role: the metal of a breastplate,",
    "the cloth of a cape. 'authored' adds ramps for materials, cloths, gems, races, the classes' and the",
    "named sets' colours (from shared/items.js CLASS_SIG and SET_THEMES): [top, middle, bottom].",
    "'family' says which roles an authored ramp can stand in for; the build adds a duller '~worn'",
    "copy of each metal, leather, cloth, fur and wood ramp (tier 0) and a '~dark' copy of each metal."
  ],
